course: dictionary
lesson: 13380
title: A word for things we wear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can work out what a new word means from the clues around it. «Mia wore a red headband to keep her hair out of her eyes.» Hair, eyes and wore tell you that a headband is something worn on the head.
explain: Read the rest of the sentence to find out its job. Mia wanted her hair away from her face, so a headband must be something that holds hair back. Check by swapping in your meaning: "Mia wore a red band of cloth around her head to keep her hair out of her eyes." It still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: A word can also show what something is for. «At the party, Sam wore a headband with bunny ears.» Party and bunny ears tell you that a headband can be for decoration and fun, not only for keeping hair back.
fact: A headband is a band of cloth, plastic or elastic worn around the head or over the hair.
fact: People wear headbands to keep hair or sweat away from the face, or for decoration.
fact: A «sweatband» is a headband worn to soak up sweat, often in sport.
fact: In crafts, pupils make paper headbands with feathers, animal ears or crowns.
fact: Useful phrases: wear a headband, a headband with ears.
exercise: «Mia wore a red headband to keep her hair out of her eyes.» What is the headband used for here? | To keep the feet warm | *To keep hair away from the face | To hold a drink | To carry books to school
exercise: Lily made a paper headband with feathers for the school play. Where is a headband worn? | Around the neck, like a scarf | Around the wrist, like a watch | *Around the head or over the hair | On the feet, like a sock
exercise: Which word means a headband worn to soak up sweat? | glove | *sweatband | scarf | sock
test: «Sam wore a headband with bunny ears to the party.» Why might Sam wear it? | *For decoration and fun | To keep his hair dry in the rain | To tie his shoes | To hold a pencil
test: Which sentence uses the word headband correctly? | The headband rang the bell at school. | Tom ate a headband for lunch. | *Tom put a headband on to keep his hair back. | Ella drank her headband with a straw.
exam: Read «Ravi wiped his face on his headband after the run.» Why was the headband probably worn? | To warm up his hands | To hold a book open | *To soak up sweat | To keep the sun off the car
